@startuml erd-overview
title Truckr® — Bounded Contexts Overview (Draft v1)

package "Identity" {
  entity "users" as user
  entity "carriers" as carrier
  entity "shippers" as shipper
  entity "vehicles" as vehicle
}

package "Marketplace" {
  entity "transport_windows" as tw
  entity "cargo_offers" as co
  entity "quotes" as quote
}

package "Fulfilment" {
  entity "shipments" as shipment
  entity "tracking_events" as te
  entity "routes" as route
}

package "Commerce" {
  entity "payments" as payment
  entity "insurance_policies" as ins
  entity "arca_invoices" as inv
}

user ||--o| carrier
user ||--o| shipper
carrier ||--o{ vehicle
carrier ||--o{ tw
vehicle ||--o{ tw
shipper ||--o{ co
co ||--o{ quote
carrier ||--o{ quote
vehicle ||--o{ quote
quote ||--o| shipment
vehicle ||--o{ shipment
shipment ||--o{ te
shipment ||--|| route
shipment ||--|| payment
shipment ||--o| ins
shipment ||--o| inv

note bottom
  Soft-deleted entities (ADR-009): shipments, payments, arca_invoices.
  Lat / lng stored as DECIMAL(9,6) columns Phase 0/1 (ADR-010).

  Cross-context Vehicle linkage: a Vehicle is committed at quote time
  (quotes.vehicle_id, NOT NULL) and frozen at acceptance into
  shipments.vehicle_id. Vehicle reassignment after acceptance is NOT
  supported in Phase 0/1 — cancel + re-quote. See domain-model.md
  §§ 2.4 / 3.3 / 4.1.

  User has no denormalised role flags — Carrier / Shipper presence is
  derived from the relation rows (ADR-008).
end note

@enduml
